    "uid": "ffe96dedb6c9f19b305fbf2f5a99bde0",
    "title": "Agent account accessed SSH files",
    "desc": "A non-human service or agent account touched an SSH file - a private key, authorized_keys, config or known_hosts. These accounts (an AI coding agent, a CI runner) have no legitimate reason to read SSH material, so any access is signal: a private key is theft, authorized_keys is a backdoor being planted, and config / known_hosts is reconnaissance for where to move next. The rule is scoped by account name because on a human login ssh reads these files constantly - it is the *who*, not the file, that makes it suspicious. Add or remove accounts in the `agent_user` selection.\nThis is an \"agentic AI detection\" rule: a detection written for the behaviour of an autonomous agent, a class SigmaHQ does not yet cover. See rules/agent/README.md.",
